# Git LFS — large committed native binaries.
#
# The Swift xcframework static libraries are CI-assembled, committed
# artifacts (assembled on macos-14 by .github/workflows/xcframework.yml when
# the uniffi FFI surface changes; refreshed via
# tooling/connect/apply-xcframework-artifact.sh), tracked via LFS so the
# repository does not accumulate ~120 MB of staticlib churn on every
# refresh. SPM consumers resolve the xcframework from git; git-lfs is bundled
# with Xcode (CLI `swift build` users run `git lfs install` once).
#
# Other Path B natives (Go `native/`, Kotlin `native/`, Python `spoke_connect/`)
# stay as plain git blobs: Go modules resolve through the module proxy (no LFS
# smudge), and the Kotlin/Python dylibs are small build inputs for the
# Maven/PyPI artifacts.
crates/spoke-connect/bindings/swift/xcframework/**/*.a filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
